<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sultan Khalil</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1478">1478</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Khalil was the eldest son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a> and briefly his successor in 1478. Formerly governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a>, he took power on his father's death, but within months he was defeated and killed by his brother Ya'qub, who then ruled until 1490.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sultan-khalil.jpg" alt="Sultan Khalil" width="320" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Chester Beatty Library, Dublin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aq_Qoyunlu_Sultan_Khalil_on_horse,_1478._Divan_of_Hidayat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
